You use data transformations on your raw data to get closer to cleaned and integrated data.
The most typical transformations are: missing or incorrect data, fixec formatting, perfom aggregations, derive new columns...
The two most common methods are SQL or Snowpark. Con Snowpark puedes usar python, java o scala.
Se pueden usar user-defined functions para reusar codigo o funciones que usas recurrentemente. UDF devuelven solo un valor.
Lo mismo con stored procedures y dynamic tables.
